				&\tilde{s}_1=\tilde{\nu}_4 \ln (4)+\frac{1}{\pi} \int_{-k_0}^{-\infty} \log _\pi \frac{\left|s-\omega k_0\right|}{\left|s-k_0\right|} \mathrm{d}\ln \left(1-\left|\tilde{r}_2(s)\right|^2\right)+\frac{1}{\pi} \int_{k_0}^{\infty} \log _0 \frac{\left|s-k_0\right|}{\left|s-\omega k_0\right|} \mathrm{d}\ln \left(1-\left|\tilde{r}_1(s)\right|^2\right),\\
				&\tilde{s}_2=\tilde{\nu}_1 \ln (4)+\frac{1}{\pi} \int_{k_0}^{\infty} \log _0 \frac{\left|s+\omega k_0\right|}{\left|s+k_0\right|} \mathrm{d}\ln \left(1-\left|\tilde{r}_1(s)\right|^2\right)+\frac{1}{\pi} \int_{-k_0}^{-\infty} \log _\pi \frac{\left|s+k_0\right|}{\left|s+\omega k_0\right|} \mathrm{d}\ln \left(1-\left|\tilde{r}_2(s)\right|^2\right).
			\end{aligned}
			$$
			{Furthermore, the asymptotic formula in Sector II holds uniformly with respect to $\xi=x / t$ in compact subset of the stated interval.}

