	The purpose of the second deformation is to expand the jumps \( v^{(1)}_{\{1,4,7,10\}} \) into regions where the $\Re{\Phi_{21}(\xi;k)}$ keeps decaying as \( t \rightarrow \infty \) for $\xi$ in some compact subset of $\R_+$, or $\Re{\tilde{\Phi}_{21}(\zeta;k)}$ keeps the decay properties as $x\to\infty$ for $\zeta\in[0,\zeta_{\rm{max}}]$. Naturally, let $U_1,U_2,\cdots,U_6$ be the open sets  defined in Figure \ref{regionU}, which are coincided with the signature of $\Re{\Phi_{21}}$.
