	%	The asymptotic of the SK(KK) equation is like the KdV equation, but the KdV equation has only one reflection coefficient with $|r(0)|=1$ and for the SK equation, there are two reflection coefficients $r_1$ and $r_2$, which also satisfy that $|r_j(0)|=1$. In the solitonless case, the KdV equation also has similar sectors and there is a collisionless region because $|r(0)|=1$, in the general case. For SK equation, the transition region between ZM region, resp. sector II, and Painlev${\rm\acute{e}}$, resp. sector IV may be  collisionless.
	%\end{remark}

