v_r
=0.5
$,~$h_\ell=\rho_\ell^{\nicefrac{3}{2}}$,~$h_r=\rho_r^{\nicefrac{3}{2}}$ and initial jump at~$x_0=0$ 
for different choices of the functions~$q(h)$,~$\h(\rho)$. 
More precisely, the panels~(i)~--~(iii) state the density~$\rho$ (blue), velocity~$v$ (red) and the driver-dependent quantity~$h$ (green) with respect to the left $y$-axis. 
The characteristic speeds~$\lambda_1(\u)$ are plotted with respect to the scale of the right $y$-axis. 
Since they are increasing, characteristics do not cross and a rarefaction wave occurs and not a shock. 
%-
Panel (vi) states the difference 
\begin{align*}
