\section{Model and Estimation}
\label{app::modest}
\subsection{State-space representation}
\label{sbapp::ssR}
In this Section, we present the complete state-space form of the two-level dynamic factor model employed for estimation, obtained by stacking the data of each group in a single $n$-dimensional vector, where $N = \sum_{c\in \mathcal{C}}\sum_{s\in \mathcal{S}} N_{c,s}$.
Without loss of generality, let us order the groups by sector. Then, the model in compact form writes as:\\
\begin{subequations}
\begin{align}
\textbf{x}_t\ &=\ \boldsymbol{\Lambda} \mathbf{F}_t + \boldsymbol{\xi}_t; \quad \xi_{i,t}\sim \mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^2_{\xi_i})\label{sbeq::compobs}\\[5pt]
\textbf{F}_t\ &=\ \mathbf{A}\mathbf{F}_t + \mathbf{u}_t; \quad  \mathbf{u}_t \sim \mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{Q})\label{sbeq::compst}
\end{align}
\end{subequations}
