        \begin{definition}
            Assume that $\cC$ is semiadditive. Let $A \in \Ab$, $\Zchar \in \Map\Enull(A, \Sigma \cC\units)$ and $W \in \Gr^{\Zchar}_A \cC$ be pointwise dualizable and with finite support. Then $W$ must be of the form $\bigoplus_{i=1}^r V_i\shift{a_i}$ for some $a_i \in A$ and $V_i \in \cC\dbl$. This defines a homomorphism $\vec{a} \colon \ZZ^r \to A$ sending $e_i$ to $a_i$. Let $W' \coloneqq \bigoplus_{i=1}^r V_i \shift{e_i} \in \Gr^{\Zchar \circ \vec{a}}_{\ZZ^r} \cC$. Then $W'$ is sent to $W$ under the symmetric monoidal functor $\vec{a}_! \colon \Gr^{\Zchar\circ \vec{a}}_{\ZZ^r} \cC \to \Gr^{\Zchar}_A \cC$. Define the braiding character of $W$ as
